      <data key="d4">Why a Coconut Is Broken at Temples and Before Every Auspicious Start A coconut gets smashed before a puja, a new business, a wedding, a journey. The gesture is so common it barely draws a glance anymore. But the tradition carries a precise meaning that most people who perform it have never been told, one that connects the fruit's anatomy to an idea about the self that runs through much of Hindu thought. ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS</data>
