      <data key="d3">en</data>
      <data key="d4">India progressing towards sending its first human deep-sea mission to depth of up to 6,000 metres by 2028: Jitendra Singh Union Minister Jitendra Singh outlined India's plans for deep-sea exploration and human spaceflight during the Indo-Pacific Regional Dialogue 2026. India intends to conduct its first human deep-sea mission by 2028, reaching depths of up to 6,000 metres. The country focuses on enhancing its capabilities through collaboration among various scientific fields. The initiative reflects India's commitment to exploring and utilizing ocean resources strategically for economic benefits.</data>
