    <node id="article:463b7e803e930ff1599a667a838ea6b0">
      <data key="d1">article</data>
      <data key="d2">463b7e803e930ff1599a667a838ea6b0</data>
      <data key="d11">SKTMCCF seeks special OTS policy for J&amp;K’s stressed business accounts</data>
      <data key="d3">en</data>
      <data key="d4">SKTMCCF seeks special OTS policy for J&amp;K’s stressed business accounts Srinagar, Nov 4: The Shahre Khass Traders, Manufacturers Coordination Committee and Federation (SKTMCCF) has urged the J&amp;K Bank to introduce a special and inclusive One-Time Settlement (OTS) policy for Non-Performing Asset (NPA) accounts in Jammu and Kashmir, saying a fair settlement framework is essential for reviving struggling businesses and protecting livelihoods. In a statement, SKTMCCF President Imtiyaz Ahmad Malik said the proposed policy should follow the State Bank of India (SBI) settlement model to ensure uniformity and uphold the principle of “One India, One Formula”. He said businesses in Jammu and Kashmir had faced prolonged economic hardships over the past several decades and deserved special revival measures to help them recover from financial distress. The committee called for special consideration for genuine business borrowers whose accounts had remained operational for years and who had regularly serviced interest obligations but eventually turned into NPAs due to circumstances beyond their control. It also sought flexible repayment timelines based on the outstanding loan amount, particularly for accounts involving dues of up to Rs 50 crore, arguing that borrowers should be given realistic opportunities to settle their liabilities. The SKTMCCF further demanded priority consideration for accounts that have remained classified as NPAs for more than seven years, saying long-pending cases required a practical settlement mechanism. The committee also listed failed OTS cases among the issues requiring attention, although it did not specify the relief or settlement terms proposed for such accounts. Malik said a fair, practical and compassionate OTS framework would help distressed traders and manufacturers settle outstanding liabilities, restart economic activity and safeguard employment. He said the revival of struggling business units would also contribute to strengthening Jammu and Kashmir’s overall economy.</data>
      <data key="d5">greaterkashmir</data>
      <data key="d6">2026-11-05 02:16:37</data>
      <data key="d12">https://www.greaterkashmir.com/business/sktmccf-seeks-special-ots-policy-for-jks-stressed-business-accounts-12784695</data>
      <data key="d13">https://greaterkashmir.com/business/sktmccf-seeks-special-ots-policy-for-jks-stressed-business-accounts-12784695</data>
